      "forbidden": ["Treating availability as adoption.", "Treating the profile as an amendment to all a_c models or a universal execution theory.", "Importing consumer identities merely through the standard."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 71,
          "quote": "Adoption of the profile is optional. The profile imports one exact `a_c` basis\nand instantiates one closed model-family signature under its record and model\nlaws. It does not amend `a_c`, become part of every `a_c` model, or define a\nuniversal execution theory.\n\nAvailability is not adoption. A Product that adopts the profile owns its\nsubject interpretation, concrete vocabulary, authorities, requirements,\ndesign, implementation, and evidence. This standard imports none of those\nconsumer identities.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/codex/5a5b5ad80f0ba4b56b83aadd42ac130de53ba803/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE_PROFILE.md#The%20%60a_c%60%20Traversal%20Occurrence%20Profile%20over%20Mutable%20Subjects%2FPosition",
